law.text:
		The Council may:

Determine standards for apprentice agreements, which standards shall not be lower than those prescribed by this article;


Appoint the secretary of the Council to act as secretary of each state joint apprenticeship committee;


Review decisions of local joint apprenticeship committees relating to apprenticeship disputes pursuant to subdivision C 3 of § 2.2-2047;


Perform such other duties as are necessary to carry out the intent of this article; and


Advise the Commissioner on policies to coordinate apprenticeship-related instruction delivered by state and local public education agencies.
